   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- **Storage:** `fieldnotes/store.py:24` saves `created` with `moment.isoformat()`. That gives a value like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`, with a timezone-aware UTC datetime.\n- **Printing:** `fieldnotes/cli.py:21` prints `note['created']` as it was stored. It doesn't reformat it, and there's no `strftime` or locale formatting anywhere in the package.\n- **Other output:** `add` prints only the note text, and the usage messages contain no dates. `list` is the only place a date is printed.\n\nI only read the code and didn't run the CLI.\n\nOne thing to watch: `list` prints whatever string is in the store. If a notes file already has entries in another format, for example from an older version or edited by hand, `list` would print them unchanged. I didn't look for existing data files. If you want a guarantee, I can add a check or normalize the value when `list` prints it.",
