   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`, which prints one `DATE: TEXT` line per note. The project checks pass: 2 tests OK and no lines over 100 characters.\n\n- **Command:** the change is in `fieldnotes/cli.py`. I also added `export` to the usage message.\n- **Date format:** `DATE` is the note's full ISO `created` timestamp, for example `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00: first`. If you want only the date part, it's a one-line change.\n- **Test:** `tests/test_cli.py` adds two notes and checks that `export` prints the expected lines and returns 0.\n- **Checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set and it wasn't, so I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory.",
